12. Article 228 of the Supreme People's Court's Opinions on Several Issues concerning the Application of the Civil Procedure Law of the People's Republic of China (Fa Fa [1992] No. 22) is adjusted as follows: "The announcement of acceptance of an application issued by the People's Court in accordance with Article 196 of the Civil Procedure Law shall specify the following contents:
(1) the name of the applicant for the public summons for exhortation;
(2) the type of instrument, the face amount, the drawer, the holder, the endorser, etc.;
(3) the period for claiming rights;
(4) the legal consequences of transferring rights in the instrument during the period of public summons for exhortation and of failure of an interested person to claim rights."

29. The first paragraph of Article 286 of the Supreme People's Court's Opinions on Several Issues concerning the Application of the Civil Procedure Law of the People's Republic of China (Fa Fa [1992] No. 22) is adjusted as follows: "Where the People's Court conducts a search of the person subject to enforcement, his domicile, or the place where property is concealed in accordance with Article 224 of the Civil Procedure Law, the following conditions must be met:
(1) the time limit for performance specified in the effective legal instrument has expired;
(2) the person subject to enforcement fails to perform the obligations specified in the legal instrument;
(3) there are grounds to believe that there is an act of concealment of property."

55. Article 102 of the Provisions of the Supreme People's Court on Several Issues Concerning the Enforcement Work of the People's Courts (for Trial Implementation) (Fa Shi [1998] No. 15) is adjusted as follows: "Under any of the following circumstances, the People's Court shall suspend enforcement in accordance with the provisions of Item 5 of Paragraph 1 of Article 232 of the Civil Procedure Law:
(1) The People's Court has accepted a bankruptcy application with the enforcement respondent as the debtor;
(2) The enforcement respondent indeed has no property available for enforcement;
(3) The subject matter of enforcement is the disputed subject matter in a case being tried by another court or arbitration institution, and the determination of ownership must await the conclusion of that case;
(4) One party applies for enforcement of an arbitral award, and the other party applies for revocation of that arbitral award;
(5) The respondent against whom enforcement of an arbitral award is sought submits a request for non-enforcement to the People's Court in accordance with the provisions of Article 213, Paragraph 2 of the Civil Procedure Law, and provides appropriate security."

60. Article 7 of the Interpretation of the Supreme People's Court on Several Issues Concerning Judicial Compensation in Civil and Administrative Proceedings (Fa Shi [2000] No. 27) is adjusted as follows: "In accordance with the provisions of Articles 17 and 31 of the State Compensation Law, the State shall not bear compensation liability under any of the following circumstances:
(1) damage caused by errors in the applicant's application for preservation;
(2) damage caused by errors in the subject matter of enforcement provided by the applicant;
(3) personal acts of the personnel of the People's Court unrelated to the exercise of their functions;
(4) circumstances falling under the provisions of Article 210 of the Civil Procedure Law;
(5) the preserved party, the enforcement respondent, or the custodian designated by the People's Court according to law illegally uses, conceals, damages, transfers, or sells property that has been preserved by the People's Court;
(6) damage caused by force majeure;
(7) other circumstances for which the State shall not bear compensation liability according to law."

66. Paragraph 1 of Article 21 of the Interpretation of the Supreme People's Court on Several Issues Concerning the Application of Law in the Trial of Labor Dispute Cases (Fa Shi [2001] No. 14) is adjusted as follows: "Where a party applies to a People's Court for enforcement of a legally effective written award or mediation statement made by a labor dispute arbitration institution, and the respondent provides evidence that the labor dispute arbitration award or mediation statement falls under any of the following circumstances, and such evidence is verified after review, the People's Court may, in accordance with the provisions of Article 213 of the Civil Procedure Law, rule to refuse enforcement:
(1) The matters adjudicated are not within the scope of labor dispute arbitration, or the labor dispute arbitration institution has no authority to arbitrate;
(2) There is indeed an error in the application of law;
(3) The arbitrator engaged in acts of favoritism or fraud or rendered an award in violation of law when arbitrating the case;
(4) The People's Court finds that enforcement of the labor dispute arbitration award would violate the social public interest."

71. Article 4 of the Provisions of the Supreme People's Court on Several Issues concerning the Trial of Cases for Confirmation of State Compensation by People's Courts (for Trial Implementation) (Fa Shi [2004] No. 10) is adjusted to: “A confirmation application falling under any of the following circumstances shall not be accepted:
(1) where a petition or application for retrial shall be filed through the trial supervision procedure according to law;
(2) where the subject matter of the application falls within a case that has been docketed and is being investigated by a judicial organ;
(3) where the act of a staff member of a People's Court is not related to the exercise of functions and powers;
(4) where it falls under the circumstances provided in Article 210 of the Civil Procedure Law of the People's Republic of China;
(5) other circumstances that are not within the scope of confirmation according to law.”
